          "message": "Signature Change: `IdentityResponder.apply_compression` and `GZipResponder.apply_compression` changed from sync to `async`, and every call site now `await`s the result. Code outside this PR that subclasses these responders and overrides `apply_compression` with a plain `def` will now fail at runtime with `TypeError: object bytes can't be used in 'await' expression`. Code that calls the method directly will get a coroutine instead of `bytes`.\n\nThis only affects users who extend these classes. Starlette documents them as non-public, so the risk is limited. If compatibility matters, consider one of these options:\n- Keep `apply_compression` sync, and add a separate async wrapper (e.g. `apply_compression_async`) that `send_with_compression` awaits.\n- Note the break in the changelog."
